---
const proofPoints = [
  'Self-hosted by default',
  'No accounts or tracking',
  'Household sharing with edit and view links',
  'Open source and MIT licensed',
];
---
<section id="top" class="relative overflow-hidden bg-gradient-to-b from-honey-50 via-cream to-white px-6 pb-20 pt-16 sm:pb-28 sm:pt-24">
  <div class="absolute inset-x-0 top-0 h-56 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_top,_rgba(245,158,11,0.18),_transparent_65%)]"></div>

  <div class="relative mx-auto grid max-w-6xl gap-14 lg:grid-cols-[1.05fr_0.95fr] lg:items-center">
    <div>
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-full border border-honey-200 bg-white px-4 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-warm-700 shadow-sm">
        <span class="h-2 w-2 rounded-full bg-honey-400"></span>
        Personal project • family-tested • packaged for other self-hosters
      </div>

      <h1 class="mt-6 text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight text-warm-900 sm:text-6xl lg:text-7xl">
        A virtual fridge door for your household
      </h1>

      <p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl leading-relaxed text-warm-700">
        Put notes, grocery lists, photos, magnets, emoji, and doodles on a shared board you run yourself. No accounts, no SaaS baggage, just one board you can share with your household.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-col items-start gap-4 sm:flex-row sm:flex-wrap">
        <a
          href="#self-host"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl bg-honey-500 px-8 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-white shadow-md transition hover:bg-honey-600 focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-honey-400 focus:ring-offset-2"
        >
          Run with Docker →
        </a>
        <a
          href="https://github.com/nacho-labs-llc/fridgeshare"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-xl border-2 border-warm-200 bg-white px-8 py-4 text-base font-semibold text-warm-800 shadow-sm transition hover:border-warm-300 hover:bg-warm-50"
        >
          View on GitHub →
        </a>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        {proofPoints.map((item) => (
          <div class="rounded-full border border-warm-200 bg-white px-4 py-2 text-sm font-medium text-warm-700 shadow-sm">
            {item}
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="rounded-[2rem] border border-warm-200 bg-white/80 p-5 shadow-[0_24px_80px_rgba(45,32,21,0.08)] backdrop-blur-sm sm:p-6">
      <div class="rounded-[1.75rem] border border-warm-100 bg-gradient-to-br from-honey-100 via-white to-warm-50 p-6">
        <div class="grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-yellow-100 p-4 shadow-sm">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-warm-700">Household board</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-lg font-semibold text-warm-900">One shared place for the little things</p>
            <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-warm-700">
              Grocery notes, pickup reminders, lunch ideas, photo drops, doodles, and magnets all stay visible together.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-warm-900 p-4 text-warm-50 shadow-sm">
            <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-honey-100">How sharing works</p>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed">
              Share the full URL with its <code class="rounded bg-white/10 px-1 py-0.5 font-mono text-xs">#token</code> to edit. Remove the fragment for read-only viewing.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="rounded-2xl bg-white p-4 shadow-sm ring-1 ring-warm-100 sm:col-span-2">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2 text-2xl">
              <span>📝</span>
              <span>🧲</span>
              <span>📸</span>
              <span>😀</span>
              <span>✏️</span>
            </div>
            <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-warm-700">
              The product stays intentionally small: create a board, keep it on your own server, and share it with the people who actually use the fridge door at home.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
